# Checked out with LF everywhere, Windows included.
#
# The tests assert bytes: a fixture's comments are compared with their offsets,
# and the NLP word lists are read line by line. Checked out with CRLF, every
# one of those strings gains a `\r` and the assertions are about a different
# file than the one that was committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-for-byte, and not text at all: a trained model and a compiled grammar.
*.bin binary
*.wasm binary
*.aff binary
*.dic binary
